  "interpretation": "protocol_b scores Node-MoE's differentiated ChebNetII pool under the same honest fixed-expert protocol as the repo's 0/234 null: the pool is routing-blind and the gate is cross-fit on disjoint nodes. faithful_joint is the paper's own end-to-end training. A win in faithful_joint but not protocol_b means the gain is co-adaptation / ensemble capacity, not genuine routing. gate_effect_joint_vs_uniform_ensemble is the causal control: it compares the gated model against the same experts combined by a fixed equal-weight mean, so a near-zero difference means the learned gate contributes nothing beyond the expert pool and averaging."
